      "note": "The beat (E2-05): each shot, and the set piece's flight, turns both drums one whole turn forward in 0.40 s, kicking fast and landing eased, so the index notch leaves the fixed index shoe and lands back under it as the stamp window opens. One row owns the drum's X turn and every turn is whole, so the notch always parks under the shoe (a free spin would leave it anywhere). A shot inside the flight adds no turn."
